ing":5,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A2U1KBDYS2OYD8\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp\"}}"},"likeCount":202,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":74},"User:149414829":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":149414829,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1753217872i/149414829._UX200_CR0,77,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":325,"textReviewsCount":155,"name":"April ","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/149414829-april","contributor":null,"id":149414829},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"default":true,"actionType":"add_to_read","sortOrder":2,"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/149414829?shelf=read"},"taggings":[],"webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5867112730"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.smpOXUobFRPj3BIEdnnqGQ":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.smpOXUobFRPj3BIEdnnqGQ","creator":{"__ref":"User:149414829"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1783684141319,"createdAt":1695732749943,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1700919311668,"text":"\u003cb\u003eA home isn’t just a place— sometimes a home is a person; sometimes a home is flesh and blood.\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eI really expected to enjoy this more. I went in with high expectations and was let down a bit. Maybe it's a me problem. I was expecting the plot to be repetitive at times with the same timeline but also wanted a new storyline with having new characters. I'm not even sure if that makes sense.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eA Soul for Revenge is the second book in the Souls Trilogy. It is an enemies to lovers, age gap, dark romance with trauma, banter, revenge, fear, and anger. I wasn't as interested in the plot as with book one and was able to see what was coming next for the most part. However, I didn't hate it and did find myself enjoying it mostly. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eJuniper Kynes was to be the first sacrifice for the God, but she escaped. Now, six years later, she returns back to Abelaum on a plan for revenge because they killed her brother to be sacrificed. She wants everyone involved dead, and what better way to do so than with a demon by her side. She had met Zane years ago, and he had been following her, but she had forgotten about him. One night, he shows up where she was, and before leaving, tell her when she is tired of running to find him. She calls upon Zane, and they make a deal her body and soul for revenge. Will they get the revenge that she seeks without being killed themselves?\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003eWhen you’re sick of running, come find me. Until then, stay alive, little wolf. I want to play with you again.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eHave I already mentioned that I hate Victoria and Jeremiah? Well, I do, especially Victoria she befriends Juniper only to stand by and help her father and his cult try to sacrifice her. I was excited to see more of Callum and Everly. We did get a little more of them with this book and what Everly strives for (and I can't wait to see what they do next). Seeing more of Rae and Leon was where it was at for side characters. I absolutely ate up the moments that we got more of Leon.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“Fix you? Ah, little wolf, I have no desire to fix you. I just want to see all your broken edges shine. I want to feel how sharp you are.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eZane and Juniper had a strong connection that built on lust at first, but it folded into more towards the second half. I didn't feel as strong of a connection as I thought I would to Juniper. One being that it seemed that for most of the first half of the book, she was either angry or afraid, and trust me, I understand both for what she went through at a young age. The second half was about her getting revenge and seeing her plan play out while she also got over some of her fears. She definitely was a badass and could take care of herself in that aspect. I'll give her that, though she didn't know when to back down and always tried to put herself in danger. I wanted to love her. I really did. But what I wanted was her anger to dissapate and for her to heal from her traumas, but her anger never allowed her to. Now Zane, I enjoyed him, but not as much as Leon (he is my number one demon). What I enjoyed most about Zane was that he was sarcastic and the cocky mouth on him was chef's kiss. I do agree that together, Zane and Juniper make the perfect team for her plan. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“Juniper Kynes, I fully intend to spend eternity showing you just how much I love you. I’ll dance in the rubble of that fucking wall forever. A demon won’t use that word unless we mean it.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSome of the things that I loved were that we got to see more of the demons in how they live. And there was a scene that stands out that we hadn't seen. Zane took Juniper to a demon night club on Earth. If you want to know more about what happens at a demons club, you will have to find out on your own. The ending was cute and refreshing to see. Please be sure to check the trigger warnings before reading. I'm ready to read Everly and Callums' story now, so off I go. \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“You can be broken,” he said. “You’ll never be too broken for me. We can be monsters; you and I. We can be wretched, messy, strange things. If you’re afraid, then you can be afraid. When you lose your light, I’ll still come back for you in the dark. You’re not alone.” He kissed my forehead. “You’ll never be alone again.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e~~~~~~~~\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eLove a good revenge story! 🤭 Let's go!","rating":3,"preReleaseBookSource":null,"shelving":{"__ref":"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A1E6M8WGOVZYBC\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp\"}}"},"likeCount":162,"viewerHasLiked":null,"commentCount":48},"User:3030788":{"__typename":"User","legacyId":3030788,"imageUrlSquare":"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/users/1767299101i/3030788._UX200_CR0,0,200,200_.jpg","isAuthor":false,"viewerRelationshipStatus":null,"followersCount":102619,"textReviewsCount":1231,"name":"Melanie (meltotheany)","webUrl":"https://www.goodreads.com/user/show/3030788-melanie-meltotheany","contributor":null,"id":3030788},"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3EJICM31LJX44":{"__typename":"User","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3EJICM31LJX44"},"Shelving:{\"creator\":{\"id\":\"kca://profile:goodreads/A3EJICM31LJX44\"},\"book\":{\"id\":\"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp\"}}":{"__typename":"Shelving","creator":{"__ref":"User:kca://profile:goodreads/A3EJICM31LJX44","id":"kca://profile:goodreads/A3EJICM31LJX44"},"book":{"__ref":"Book:kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp","id":"kca://book/amzn1.gr.book.v3.HAb8vYyZpBmDQGSp"},"shelf":{"__typename":"Shelf","name":"read","displayName":"Read","editable":false,"defaul