Stars *:･ﾟ✧\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\u003cb\u003e\u003ci\u003eI squat down, glaring into her smug, beautiful face. “I haven’t even begun to wreck you, girl. You think you won this round? You’ve only made me crave breaking you more.” \u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eShe grinned, flipping me off from the floor. “I’ve already wrecked you, demon boy. Round one goes to me.\"\u003c/i\u003e\u003c/b\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e━━━━━━━━━━━ ♡ ━━━━━━━━━━━\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eReread this last night so now you all get a proper review 😘. Ask me how much I'd pay for her to call me 'demon boy'. She's so? This book was absolutely fabulous, as expected. Harley Laroux continues to blow my expectations out of the water. Although Leon still remains my fav mans, my girl Juniper can get it \u003ci\u003eany\u003c/i\u003e time.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eThis book does not take place after the first book, it is about Juniper and Zane during the plot of the first book. So, you see all the events that took place in the first book through a different lense and through different character involvement. I absolutely (unsurprisingly) loved it. I love this world so much and the characters are just perfect. I 100% recommend you check trigger warnings when looking to read this series, and it \u003cu\u003eis\u003c/u\u003e a dark romance, but I never felt weighed down by the intensity. Rather, it had it's steaming hot, to die for moments, but also had the most perfect romance. I also really appreciate when dark romance still makes use of safewords. Juniper and Zane's safeword is 'mercy'; super cute, and it's integrated perfectly.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003ci\u003e“As if you want me to be nice,” she ground out the words, snarling furiously as she thrashed beneath me. She was right — this was exactly how I liked her. Righteously angry, proudly in denial that every choice she made was bringing he