review/show/4627688336"},"Review:kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.DsvxCj6iAQuX0m_K-LbbDA":{"__typename":"Review","id":"kca://review:goodreads/amzn1.gr.review:goodreads.v1.DsvxCj6iAQuX0m_K-LbbDA","creator":{"__ref":"User:15335689"},"recommendFor":null,"updatedAt":1732621356346,"createdAt":1654408246778,"spoilerStatus":false,"lastRevisionAt":1669652535456,"text":"\u003cblockquote\u003e#1 \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4264036975\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eHer Soul to Take\u003c/a\u003e ★★★★★\u003cbr /\u003e#1 \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4627688336\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eHer Soul for Revenge\u003c/a\u003e ★★★★★\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cb\u003e“If the woods call your name, don’t answer. Run.”\u003c/b\u003e\u003c/blockquote\u003e \u003cbr /\u003eShould I have reviewed this \u003ci\u003emonths\u003c/i\u003e ago, when I first read it? Yes. Am I going to try my best to do this book justice anyways, despite my terrible memory, because these characters and this series deserves the best? Also yes. I love this series and this world so damn much, and I think about these characters pretty much every day (mostly thinking about how badly I hope book 3 comes out soon, because I NEED IT).\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eThere are places on Earth that are cursed all the way down to their roots. Places that hold pain, that tasted blood and can’t get enough. Places where darkness grows, and even in daylight, they lie under a shadow.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAs I mentioned in my review of \u003ci\u003eHer Soul to Take,\u003c/i\u003e most romance books with horror themes don't hit it for me as a horror lover, but \u003cb\u003eHarley Laroux gets it.\u003c/b\u003e The horror elements, the demon lore, the violence and descriptions of these awful beasties in the woods, all of it is so on point and I love it. It has the best folk horror vibes and I'm here for it always. If you're a horror lover who's considering trying out romance (or a romance lover who's considering trying out horror!), I genuinely feel like this series is a fantastic merging of the two.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eSurvival is messy. Survival has no morals or kindness. Survival isn’t black and white, good versus evil. Survival is shades of red; it’s blood taken and blood lost.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eSpeaking of things Harley Laroux clearly \"gets\", I could gush for a long damn time about the PTSD and trauma rep in this book. Juniper's PTSD is beautifully well-written and I related to her so many times, so I loved this over-arching theme of healing on our own time, not being forced through it, and not being made to feel guilty for the ways in which we cope in the meantime. Zane adds so much to this, too; he's never Juniper's \"savior\", he's just there to help where he can, and to be there for her. Everyone needs someone like that in their life and I adored every single bit of dialogue between the two of them regarding her trauma and healing.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003eMonsters were real and Gods were evil, so the world was already going to Hell, regardless of my weird sexual turn-ons.\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eOne thing everyone should know going into this series, though, is that it's a remarkably dark and heavy read at times. The content warnings are extensive and some of them are a bit unusual. I love the way Harley writes BDSM in healthy relationships and how strong the focus is on consent and safety, but it's not for everyone—and there are some kinks explored in these pages (minor spoiler: \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"fae62be7-2ebe-4edd-8fa0-7be6d88f81fa\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"fae62be7-2ebe-4edd-8fa0-7be6d88f81fa\"\u003esuch as sex beside a freshly murdered corpse!\u003c/label\u003e) that aren't going to fly with some readers. \u003ci\u003e(Not sure what it says about me that I was so delighted by that particular scene, but it was cathartic and I cheered a little.)\u003c/i\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cblockquote\u003e\n  \u003cb\u003e“Fix you? Ah, little wolf, I have no desire to fix you. I just want to see all your broken edges shine. I want to feel how sharp you are. ”\u003c/b\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eAll of that aside, I could go on for another nine paragraphs about how much I love Zane and Juniper, how thoroughly Zane checks all my boxes for my \u003ci\u003efavorite\u003c/i\u003e romance hero archetypes, how badass and brave Juniper is, or how invested I was in their romance, but I'll stop here and simply say that I truly hope more people check out this series and give Harley Laroux the love she deserves, because I am obsessed with the \u003ci\u003eSouls\u003c/i\u003e trilogy and I NEED more of it in my life.\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003eBuddy read with \u003ca href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/4627376166\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\"\u003eMalli\u003c/a\u003e! ♥\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e✨ \u003cb\u003eRepresentation:\u003c/b\u003e Juniper and Zane are queer; multiple BIPOC and queer side characters; Juniper has PTSD\u003cbr /\u003e\u003cbr /\u003e✨ \u003cb\u003eContent warnings\u003c/b\u003e for: \u003cinput type=\"checkbox\" class=\"spoiler__control\" aria-label=\"The following text has been marked spoiler. Toggle checkbox to reveal or hide.\" onchange=\"this.labels[0].setAttribute('aria-hidden', !this.checked);\" id=\"1a90c529-9217-4f6a-b7d8-2d2d069da70d\" /\u003e\u003clabel aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"spoiler\" for=\"1a90c529-9217-4f6a-b7d8-2d2d0